Step 1: Load Data
First, load the relevant MIMIC-IV tables from their CSV files.

python
Copy code
import pandas as pd

# Load CSV files
patients = pd.read_csv('patients.csv')
admissions = pd.read_csv('admissions.csv')
diagnoses_icd = pd.read_csv('diagnoses_icd.csv')
icustays = pd.read_csv('icustays.csv')
chartevents = pd.read_csv('chartevents.csv')
d_items = pd.read_csv('d_items.csv')
Step 2: Filter for Diabetes Diagnoses
Filter diagnoses_icd for relevant ICD codes (diabetes) and merge with admissions and patients.

python
Copy code
# Filter for diabetes ICD codes
diabetes_codes = diagnoses_icd[
    (diagnoses_icd['icd_code'].str.startswith('250')) |  # ICD-9
    (diagnoses_icd['icd_code'].str.startswith('E1'))    # ICD-10
]

# Merge with admissions and patients
diabetes_patients = diabetes_codes.merge(admissions, on='hadm_id').merge(patients, on='subject_id')

# Calculate approximate year of birth
diabetes_patients['approx_year_of_birth'] = diabetes_patients['anchor_year'] - diabetes_patients['anchor_age']
Step 3: Add ICU Events
Filter ICU events (chartevents) for glucose-related entries and join with diabetes patients.

python
Copy code
# Filter d_items for glucose-related items
glucose_items = d_items[d_items['label'].str.contains('glucose', case=False)]

# Filter chartevents for glucose events
glucose_events = chartevents[chartevents['itemid'].isin(glucose_items['itemid'])]

# Merge ICU stays with glucose events
icu_diabetes_events = icustays.merge(glucose_events, on='stay_id')

# Merge ICU data with diabetes patient data
final_data = diabetes_patients.merge(icu_diabetes_events, on='hadm_id', how='inner')
